### Day 01: Spring Boot with Kotlin - Interactive REST Client
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Create a New Product (Returns 201 Created + Location Header)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "SKU-KEY-0001",
  "name": "Mechanical Gaming Keyboard",
  "description": "RGB backlight with tactile blue mechanical switches",
  "price": 129.99,
  "stockQuantity": 50,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 2. Create Another Product
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "SKU-MOU-0002",
  "name": "Wireless Precision Mouse",
  "description": "Ergonomic ultra-lightweight optical gaming mouse",
  "price": 79.99,
  "stockQuantity": 120,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 3. Get Product By ID (Returns 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1
Accept: application/json

### 4. Get All Products (Returns 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Accept: application/json
